# Workflow: Mobile Build Simulation

Spec: MobileBuild

Purpose:
  Defines the mobile build simulation workflow within SDDRA.
  Since SDDRA is a specification framework (not a mobile app),
  the "build" generates mock APK/IPA artifacts to validate
  chain execution and demonstrate the MD branch of the
  delivery chain (BC→BR→BD→DS→TK→BDD→MD→MD_TS→CR).

Owns: workflow\mobile-build.sdd

SimulationPipeline:
  trigger: /sdd "simulate mobile build" or docker compose run mobile-builder
  stages:
    - PREPARE
    - DEPENDENCIES
    - COMPILE (simulated)
    - BUNDLE (simulated)
    - SIGN (simulated)
    - OUTPUT

  PREPARE:
    action: Validate mobile profile in .sdd/project/profile.sdd
    check: MD field must be set (React Native, Flutter, SwiftUI, KMP)
    gate: If no MD profile → return error, no build

  DEPENDENCIES:
    action: npm ci inside mobile-builder container
    mount: ./var/mobile-build:/workspace
    check: package.json exists, node_modules installed

  COMPILE:
    action: Simulate native compilation
    detail: |
      React Native: generate mock .jsbundle files
      Flutter: generate mock .app artifacts
      SwiftUI: generate mock .ipa placeholder
      KMP: generate platform-specific placeholders
    note: NO actual SDK required — pure simulation

  BUNDLE:
    action: Bundle assets and resources
    output: assets.zip in ./var/mobile-build/output/

  SIGN:
    action: Generate mock signature checksum
    detail: SHA-256 hash of the unsigned artifact (not real signing)
    note: Clearly labeled as "MOCK SIGNATURE — NOT CRYPTOGRAPHIC"

  OUTPUT:
    action: Generate build report and summary
    files:
      - app.android.apk (mock)
      - app.ios.ipa (mock)
      - bundle.<platform>.jsbundle (mock)
      - assets.zip (mock)
      - build-report.json (real, metadata only)
      - summary.txt (human-readable)

Rules:
  [MB-01] Mobile build simulation runs EXCLUSIVELY in Docker (R102).
  [MB-02] All artifacts in ./var/mobile-build/output/ (R92).
  [MB-03] Every artifact MUST be labeled "MOCK BUILD" or "SIMULATION".
  [MB-04] Build report is real metadata — artifact sizes, timestamps.
  [MB-05] No Android SDK, Xcode, or native toolchains required.
  [MB-06] Simulation MUST complete within 60 seconds.
  [MB-07] Build report MUST be valid JSON.
  [MB-08] If mobile profile is missing, return error — do NOT proceed.
  [MB-09] Artifacts MUST be deleted per tmp discipline after use ([R96]).

MDExecutionChain:
  MD:
    description: Mobile development branch in DL1 delivery chain
    entry: BDD → MD (mobile scenarios derived from BDD)
    exit: MD_TS → CR → AN
    builder: mobile-builder (Docker service)
    artifacts: ./var/mobile-build/output/
    gate: Build report validation, NOT real binary verification

State: +
